## TIẾNG ANH · 16:30–17:00 — Thứ Ba: Giải thích khái niệm

### 16:30–16:40 · Shadowing

### 16:40–16:55 · Nói to có ghi âm

**Chủ đề: bạn xử lý xung đột cử chỉ như thế nào.**

> *"The hard part of gestures isn't the gesture — it's deciding who wins when two of them want the same touch.*
> *In my list, three things compete: the list scrolling vertically, a horizontal swipe to delete, and a tap to open the detail screen.*
> *For scroll versus swipe, I use activation thresholds. The pan gesture only activates after fifteen points of horizontal movement, and it fails outright if there's more than ten points of vertical movement first. So an ambiguous diagonal drag resolves to scrolling, which is what people expect — scrolling is the primary interaction and the swipe is secondary.*
> *For swipe versus tap, I compose them as exclusive with the pan first, so a tap only fires if the pan never activated.*
> *One thing I'd call out on the design side: I also decide on velocity, not just distance. A short fast flick should delete. If you only check how far they dragged, the interaction feels heavy.*
> *And the swipe isn't the only way to delete. It's a hidden gesture — screen reader users can't perform it, and people don't discover it on their own. Long press still opens a menu, and there's an accessibility action registered on the row."*

### 16:55–17:00 · 5 từ mới

| Từ / cụm | Nghĩa | Câu mẫu |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `compete for` | tranh giành | *Three things compete for the same touch.* |
| `activation threshold` | ngưỡng kích hoạt | *I use activation thresholds.* |
| `resolve to` | ngã ngũ thành | *An ambiguous drag resolves to scrolling.* |
| `flick` (n) | cú vẩy nhanh | *A short fast flick should delete.* |
| `call out` (v) | nhấn mạnh, nêu rõ | *One thing I'd call out.* |

